# TypeScript Rules

- Prefer explicit interfaces and types for public contracts.
- Keep classes small and constructor dependencies explicit.
- Do not instantiate infrastructure inside use cases or controllers.
- Prefer domain value objects over primitives when a value has domain meaning.
- Keep DTOs in the application layer and HTTP schemas in presentation.
- Run `pnpm typecheck` after meaningful TypeScript changes.
- Do not introduce framework-specific types outside the layer that owns the framework.
- Preserve existing file naming conventions: `*.usecase.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.repository.ts`, `*.mapper.ts`, `*.port.ts`.
